Suppose a large group of people in a room were all born in the same year. Each of the following algorithms is intended to identify the people with the earliest birthday, based on month and day. For example, February 10 is earlier than March 5. Which algorithms will identify the correct people?
&lt;div class=&quot;algorithm&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;I.&lt;/b&gt; Everyone stands. Standing people form pairs where possible. In each pair, the person with the earlier birthday remains standing and the other sits down; if tied, both sit down. An unpaired person remains standing. Repeat until one person remains; identify that person.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;algorithm&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;II.&lt;/b&gt; Everyone stands. Standing people form pairs with someone they have not previously been paired with where possible. In each pair, the person with the earlier birthday remains standing and the other sits down; if tied, both remain standing. An unpaired person remains standing. Repeat until only one person remains or all standing people have the same birthday; identify everyone still standing.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;algorithm&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;III.&lt;/b&gt; Starting with 1, ask if anyone was born on that day of any month. Increase the day until someone responds. If one person responds, identify that person; otherwise identify the responder(s) born in the earliest month.&lt;/div&gt;

An algorithm will identify the maximum value in a list of one or more integers. Consider these versions:
&lt;div class=&quot;algorithm&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Algorithm I:&lt;/b&gt; Set max to −1. Iterate through the list. If a data value is greater than max, set max to that data value.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;algorithm&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Algorithm II:&lt;/b&gt; Set max to the first data value. Iterate through the remaining values. If a data value is greater than max, set max to that data value.&lt;/div&gt;
Which statement best describes the behavior of the two algorithms?
